BUG CLASS JUST FOUND AND FIXED (one instance):
In C, an `enum` whose enumerators are ALL non-negative gets an UNSIGNED underlying type under GCC. So a RELATIONAL comparison (`<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=`) involving an enum-typed value is an UNSIGNED comparison. When a caller passes a negative int across the FFI boundary into such an enum parameter/field, the C compares it as a huge unsigned value.

Concrete instance already fixed: `LZ4F_optimalBSID` (c_src/src/lz4frame.c:359-371) does `while (requestedBSID > proposedBSID)` where `requestedBSID` is `LZ4F_blockSizeID_t`. The Rust had `while requestedBSID > proposedBSID` with `c_int` (SIGNED) and diverged for blockSizeID = -1000. Fixed to `while (requestedBSID as c_uint) > (proposedBSID as c_uint)` in translation/src/lz4frame.rs.

YOUR JOB: find EVERY OTHER instance of this same bug class, plus the closely-related signed/unsigned mismatch classes, and fix ONLY the Rust.

STEP 1 - Enumerate the C enum types and whether each is unsigned (all enumerators >= 0):
  grep -n 'typedef enum' -A 12 c_src/include/lz4frame.h c_src/include/lz4.h c_src/include/lz4hc.h c_src/include/xxhash.h
  Also check enums declared inside c_src/src/*.c (grep -n 'typedef enum' -A 10 c_src/src/*.c).
  Note: LZ4F_blockSizeID_t, LZ4F_blockMode_t, LZ4F_contentChecksum_t, LZ4F_blockChecksum_t, LZ4F_frameType_t, LZ4F_errorCodes, XXH_errorcode, and the internal enums in lz4.c/lz4hc.c/lz4frame.c (limitedOutput_directive, tableType_t, dict_directive, dictIssue_directive, earlyEnd_directive, decode_directive, variable_length_error, LZ4F_BlockCompressMode_e, dStage_t, LZ4HC_strat_e, etc.).

STEP 2 - For every RELATIONAL comparison, min/max, or arithmetic in the C that involves an enum-typed operand, or a `size_t`/`unsigned` vs `int` mixed comparison, locate the Rust counterpart and verify the signedness matches. Use targeted greps, e.g.:
  grep -n 'blockSizeID\|blockMode\|frameType\|contentChecksumFlag\|blockChecksumFlag\|dictID' c_src/src/lz4frame.c
  grep -n 'compressionLevel' c_src/src/lz4frame.c
  and the matching identifiers in translation/src/lz4frame.rs.
Pay particular attention to:
  a) `LZ4F_getBlockSize` (lz4frame.c:333): `if (blockSizeID < LZ4F_max64KB || blockSizeID > LZ4F_max4MB)` -- UNSIGNED. Verify the Rust reaches the same verdict for negative and huge inputs (it may already, via the other half of the ||, but confirm the RETURN value and any subsequent index arithmetic match).
  b) `LZ4F_compressBound_internal` / `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` block-size derivation for out-of-range blockSizeID.
  c) Any place a `& _1BIT` / `& _2BITS` / `& _3BITS` mask is applied to a possibly-negative field (masking is sign-agnostic for the low bits, but the surrounding comparison may not be).
  d) `LZ4F_decodeHeader` field extraction (lz4frame.c:1348-1430) -- these come from bytes so are non-negative; lower priority.
  e) lz4.c / lz4hc.c: `acceleration` and `compressionLevel` are plain `int` (SIGNED) -- confirm the Rust keeps them signed. Also `LZ4_compress_generic`'s `(unsigned)srcSize > (unsigned)LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` style casts and `LZ4HC_getCLevelParams`'s `if (cLevel < 1)` (SIGNED).

