[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    258[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Real translation bug found and fixed by Phase C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    259[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    260[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `LZ4F_optimalBSID` (`c_src/src/lz4frame.c:359-371`) compares
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    261[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `requestedBSID > proposedBSID`. `LZ4F_blockSizeID_t` declares only non-negative
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    262[0m:[38;5;10m[49m enumerators, so under GCC its underlying type is **`unsigned int`** and that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    263[0m:[38;5;10m[49m comparison is **unsigned**. A negative `blockSizeID` arriving across the FFI
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    264[0m:[38;5;10m[49m boundary therefore compares as a huge value, enters the loop, and is clamped to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    265[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `LZ4F_max64KB` (4).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    266[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
