[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    268[0m:[38;5;10m[49m unchanged and the emitted BD header byte was `0x00` instead of `0x40` (and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    269[0m:[38;5;10m[49m header checksum followed it). Fixed in `translation/src/lz4frame.rs:401`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    270[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    271[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    272[0m:[38;5;10m[49m while (requestedBSID as c_uint) > (proposedBSID as c_uint) {
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    273[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    274[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    275[0m:[38;5;10m[49m A follow-up audit of every C enum in the tree (all 23 have non-negative-only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    276[0m:[38;5;10m[49m enumerators, hence unsigned) and every relational comparison involving one found
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    277[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no further instances; `LZ4F_getBlockSize`'s `(v < 4 || v > 7)` reaches the same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    278[0m:[38;5;10m[49m verdict under either signedness, and `acceleration` / `compressionLevel` are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    279[0m:[38;5;10m[49m plain `int` in the C and correctly signed in the Rust.
