[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    358[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    359[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Test-harness contract violations found while writing Phase B
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    360[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    361[0m:[38;5;10m[49m These were bugs in the *tests*, not the translation, and each is now documented
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    362[0m:[38;5;10m[49m in the test that hit it. They are recorded because in every case both libraries
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    363[0m:[38;5;10m[49m misbehaved *identically at first glance* while diverging for reasons unrelated to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    364[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the translation — exactly the kind of false positive that wastes a debugging pass:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    365[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    366[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **Freed source blocks between `_continue` calls.** `lz4.h:431` — "The previous
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    367[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    64KB of source data is __assumed__ to remain present, unmodified, at same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    368[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    address in memory!" (and `lz4hc.h:134` for HC). Dropping a block is a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    369[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    use-after-free; the C and Rust `.so`s have independent allocators, so they
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    370[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    read different residual bytes out of the freed dictionary tail. Fixed with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    371[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `common::BlockArena`, which parks every block for the life of the stream.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    372[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **Zero-capacity `Vec` as a `src` pointer.** `Vec::new().as_ptr()` is a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    373[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    dangling non-null pointer; the level-10+ optimal parser reached through
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    374[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize` dereferences `src` before consulting `srcSize`, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    375[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    both libraries segfault. `common::mkdata` now always backs the slice with at
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    376[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    least 64 zero-initialised bytes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    377[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. **`LZ4_compress_forceExtDict` is `notLimited`** (4 args, no `dstCapacity`), so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    378[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `dst` must be at least `LZ4_compressBound(srcSize)`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    379[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. **`LZ4_compressHC2_continue` after `LZ4_slideInputBufferHC`.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    380[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast` sets `prefixStart = NULL`, and the degraded
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    381[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `HC2_continue` path calls `LZ4HC_compress_generic` directly without the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    382[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    auto-init that `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` performs — the C nul-derefs.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    383[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. **`LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` requires `LZ4F_blockIndependent`**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    384[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`lz4frame.h:707`) and `dstCapacity >= srcSize` (`lz4frame.h:701`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    385[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 6. **`stableDst` requires a persistent output buffer.** The pledge is that the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    386[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    previously decoded 64 KB sits immediately before `dstBuffer`; handing the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    387[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    decoder a fresh allocation each call makes both libraries produce the same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    388[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    wrong bytes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    389[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 7. **`frameInfo.frameType` is a read-only field** (`lz4frame.h:177`): setting it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    390[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    does not make `LZ4F_compressFrame` emit a skippable frame.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    391[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 8. **`LZ4F_readOpen` `fread`s the full 19-byte `LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MAX`**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    392[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`lz4file.c:92`), so frames for tiny payloads legitimately fail with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    393[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `ERROR_io_read`.
